Falsifies `system_tests::user::compositor_tests::a_lying_damage_rectangle_changes_nothing_of_its_neighbours`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: the compositor writes the commit's `STATUS` word into the **last** client's control page
instead of the committing client's. A confused deputy of the smallest kind: the address the
compositor writes is no longer a function of whose frame it is serving, and a client that lies about
its rectangle gets the compositor to write `STATUS_CLIPPED` into a neighbour's memory.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(w.client_control_words(VICTIM), ctl, "a neighbour's lying rectangle
changed the victim's control page ...")`. Measured 2026-10-03 (UTC): red, the victim's `STATUS`
word (index 5) reads 1 where it read 0.

The victim's pixel digest stays equal under this patch, which is why the witness is the whole
control page and not only the surface: the compositor writes only control pages, so that is where
this class of defect lands. The surface assertion beside it is the half this patch does not reach.

Re-cut 2026-10-04 (UTC) by `lane/fuzz-service-handlers`, when the status word's value moved into
`compositor::commit_damage` and `serve_frame` kept only the store; the defect is the same store to
the same wrong page. That lane did not replay it under QEMU; the weekly sweep does.

diff --git a/components/src/compositor.rs b/components/src/compositor.rs
index 38a1224be..947d8d2b9 100644
--- a/components/src/compositor.rs
+++ b/components/src/compositor.rs
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@ fn serve_frame(
             rd32(c + ctl::DAMAGE_W),
             rd32(c + ctl::DAMAGE_H),
         );
-        wr32(c + ctl::STATUS, status);
+        wr32(ctl_va(n - 1) + ctl::STATUS, status);
         damage = damage.union(&seen);
         wr32(c + ctl::ACKED, seq);
     }
